question:
A target consists of four concentric circles with radii 4 inches, 6 inches, 8 inches and 10 inches as shown. Given that a dart is thrown that hits the target at a random point, what is the probability that it hits a shaded region? Express your answer as a common fraction.

[asy]size(100); import graph; fill(Circle((0,0),5),gray(.6));

clip(Circle((0,0),2) ^^ Circle((0,0),3) ^^ Circle((0,0),4),fillrule(1));
draw(Circle((0,0),2) ^^ Circle((0,0),3) ^^ Circle((0,0),4) ^^ Circle((0,0),5));[/asy]

Circles with centers at $O$ and $P$ have radii 2 and 4, respectively, and are externally tangent. Points $A$ and $B$ on the circle with center $O$ and points  $C$ and $D$ on the circle with center $P$ are such that  $\overline{AD}$ and $\overline{BC}$ are common external tangents to the circles. What is the area of the concave hexagon $AOBCPD$?

[asy]
pair A,B,C,D,H,O,P;
O = (0,0);
P = (6,0);
H = (-6,0);
A = intersectionpoint(arc((A + H)/2, abs(A -  H)/2, 0, 180), arc(O, 2, 0, 180));
D = intersectionpoint(arc((A + P)/2, abs(A -  P)/2, 0, 180), arc(P, 4, 0, 180));
B = reflect(O,P)*(A);
C = reflect(O,P)*(D);
draw(O--P,linewidth(0.7));
draw(Circle(O,2),linewidth(0.7));
draw(Circle(P,4),linewidth(0.7));
draw(interp(A,D,-0.2)--interp(A,D,1.2),linewidth(0.7));
draw(interp(B,C,-0.2)--interp(B,C,1.2),linewidth(0.7));
draw(A--O--B,linewidth(0.7));
draw(D--P--C,linewidth(0.7));
label("$O$",O,SE);
label("$P$",P,E);
label("$D$",D,NW);
label("$A$",A,NW);
label("$B$",B,S);
label("$C$",C,S);
label("2",(-0.45,0.95),E);
label("6",(3,0),N);
label("4",(5.55,1.95),E);

[/asy]

All of the triangles in the figure and the central hexagon are equilateral. Given that $\overline{AC}$ is 3 units long, how many square units, expressed in simplest radical form, are in the area of the entire star? [asy]
import olympiad; import geometry; import graph; size(150); defaultpen(linewidth(0.8));
pair[] vertices;
for(int i = 0; i < 6; ++i){

vertices[i] = dir(30 + 60*i);
}
draw(vertices[0]--vertices[2]--vertices[4]--cycle);
draw(vertices[1]--vertices[3]--vertices[5]--cycle);
label("$D$",vertices[0],NE); label("$C$",vertices[1],N); label("$B$",vertices[2],NW); label("$A$",vertices[3],SW);
label("$F$",vertices[4],S); label("$E$",vertices[5],SE);
[/asy]

