Equilateral triangle $DEF$ is inscribed in equilateral triangle $ABC$ as shown with $\overline{ED}\perp\overline{BC}.$ What is the ratio of the area of $\triangle DEF$ to the area of $\triangle
ABC$? [asy]
import olympiad; import geometry; size(100); defaultpen(linewidth(0.8));
draw(dir(90)--dir(210)--(dir(-30))--cycle);
pair[] inters = intersectionpoints(Circle(origin,1/sqrt(3)),dir(90)--dir(210)--(dir(-30))--cycle);
inters[5] = dir(210) + ((dir(-30) - dir(210))/3);
draw(inters[0]--inters[2]--inters[5]--cycle);
draw(rightanglemark(inters[2],inters[5],dir(210),4));
dot("$A$",dir(90),N);
dot("$C$",dir(210),W);
dot("$B$",dir(-30),E);
dot("$F$",inters[0],E);
dot("$E$",inters[2],W);
dot("$D$",inters[5],S);
[/asy]

The foci of the ellipse $\frac{x^2}{49} + \frac{y^2}{33} = 1$ are $F_1$ and $F_2,$ as shown below.  Let $P$ be a point on the circle $x^2 + (y - 3)^2 = 4.$  Line $F_2 P$ intersects the ellipse again at $Q,$ where the $y$-coordinate of $Q$ is positive.  Find the maximum value of $PQ + F_1 Q.$

[asy]
unitsize(0.4 cm);

pair P, Q;
pair[] F;

path ell = yscale(sqrt(33))*xscale(7)*Circle((0,0),1);
F[1] = (4,0);
F[2] = (-4,0);
P = (0,3) + 2*dir(240);
Q = intersectionpoint(P--interp(F[2],P,5),ell);

draw(ell);
draw((-8,0)--(8,0));
draw((0,-7)--(0,7));
draw(Circle((0,3),2));
draw(F[1]--Q--F[2]);

dot("$F_1$", F[1], S);
dot("$F_2$", F[2], S);
dot("$P$", P, S);
label("$Q$", Q, NE);
[/asy]

For $x \ge 1,$ let $f$ be the function defined as follows:
\[f(x) = \left\{
\begin{array}{cl}
\lfloor x \rfloor \left| x - \lfloor x \rfloor - \dfrac{1}{2 \lfloor x \rfloor} \right| & \text{if $x < \lfloor x \rfloor + \dfrac{1}{\lfloor x \rfloor}$}, \\
f \left( x - \dfrac{1}{\lfloor x \rfloor} \right) & \text{otherwise}.
\end{array}
\right.\]Let $g(x) = 2^{x - 2007}.$ Compute the number of points in which the graphs of $f$ and $g$ intersect.

